jobs.description:
Headit is looking for a driven Business Development Representative for an international organisation and market leader in professional legal and tax software solutions.


With these digital tools, they support knowledge professionals such as lawyers, accountants and in-house legal teams in making their daily work easier and more efficient.


Where will you work?


You will join a modern, international environment with a strong focus on digital innovation.

You will work closely with colleagues in sales, marketing and product teams, and you can choose to work from either Berchem or Louvain-La-Neuve.

Hybrid working (up to 3 days from home) and flexible working hours are standard within the company.


Your role as Business Development Representative:


As a Business Development Representative, you play a key role in proactively identifying and approaching prospects, as well as scheduling meetings and calls for the sales teams. In close collaboration with sales and marketing, you are responsible for contacting prospects and existing customers by phone, email and social media. In doing so, you actively contribute to pipeline growth and support the commercial teams in achieving their targets.



• Act as the first point of contact for outbound leads, ensuring fast and professional follow-up; 

• Schedule qualified meetings and calls for the sales team, including relevant context and information; 

• Qualify prospects based on predefined criteria; 

• Use the CRM system accurately and keep contact information up to date; 

• Regularly align with sales and marketing on pipeline development and optimisation opportunities; 


• Proven experience in a BDR, SDR or similar role with a strong outbound/commercial focus; 

• Fluency in French and English, both spoken and written; 

• Experience working with CRM systems; 

• A strong and persuasive communicator, especially over the phone; 

• Proactive, independent and results-oriented; 

• A team player who collaborates easily with different internal teams.

To strengthen our Supply Chain Department we are looking for a LOGISTICS TEAM LEADER:

Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is a subsidiary of Safran Aircraft Engines, based at Brussels Airport (Zaventem & Steenokkerzeel, Belgium), specialized in the inspection, maintenance and repair (MRO) of the advanced LEAP jet engines that power the latest generation of the Airbus A320NEO & Boeing B737MAX narrow body families. The company is a key player in the integrated CFM international MRO network. With more than 75 years of experience, and up to 20 international Part 145 certifications (EASA/ FAA/ CAAC/ …), Safran Aircraft Engine Services Brussels is recognized as a worldwide center of expertise in the air transport industry. More than a 100 airlines, lessors, private aircraft operators and MRO partners have entrusted their engines to our company. We employ over 500 highly skilled, passionate and enthusiastic employees.

Your role:

• You are a point of contact for our transport partners;
• You lead a team of 10 logistics colleagues;
• You provide support for your team by developing their knowledge in cooperation with your manager;
• You propose relevant KPI's and create reports for the activity;
• You lead the daily activity meeting together with your manager;
• You follow the work and safety instructions specifically to the workstation and the company;
• You respect the internal quality regulations and the rules of logistics and administrative management of the company;
• You inspire and enthuse employees and stimulate teamwork;
• You take initiatives and make proposals in a context of continuous improvement, pro-actively evaluates, coordinates the improvement of current work methods and introduces new technologies as they arise;
• You maintain constructive and effective relations within and outside the company.

Your profile:

• You hold at least a Bachelor in Supply Chain or Logistics, or a technical education in Logistics with experience, or you have demonstrated experience as a Team Leader;
• You have at least 5 years of experience in team management;
• You demonstrate good communication skills, good practical sense and a sense of initiative while anticipating and taking part in the context of continuous improvement;
• You have a good team spirit and are open and adaptable;
• You speak Dutch, French and are fluent in English;
• You have a good knowledge of IT tools (MS Office + ERP). SAP is a plus

Candidates must be legally authorized to work in Belgium, holding either an EU passport or a valid work & residence permit. Please note that we do not provide assistance with visa or permit applications.

Bedrijfsomschrijving 

Our client is an innovative and growing production company specializing in large-format digital printing and visual communication products. To strengthen the printing department, we are looking for a motivated Digital Print Operator who enjoys working with modern technology and delivering high-quality results.

As a Digital Print Operator, you will be responsible for operating and monitoring advanced digital printing machines. After a thorough internal training period, you will gradually learn to work independently and take ownership of the printing process.

Your responsibilities include:


• 
Operating and setting up large-format digital printers;


• 
Monitoring production progress and ensuring print quality throughout the process;


• 
Changing rolls and materials using ergonomic tools and equipment;


• 
Performing routine maintenance on the machines;


• 
Troubleshooting minor technical issues independently;


• 
Collaborating closely with colleagues and the production manager;


• 
Ensuring a safe, clean and organized workplace;


• 
Contributing ideas to improve quality, efficiency, safety and environmental performance.

We are looking for a hands-on and detail-oriented colleague who:


• 
Has technical affinity or experience in a printing or production environment;


• 
Is comfortable working with modern machinery and computer systems;


• 
Works accurately and has a strong eye for quality;


• 
Is proactive and enjoys solving problems;


• 
Can work independently as well as in a team;


• 
Is organized, reliable and punctual;


• 
Has a very good command of English or Dutch, both spoken and written;


• 
Feels comfortable working in a dynamic SME environment;


• 
Is physically fit and able to handle material changes when required;


• 
Is willing to work in a day shift (preferably 07:00 – 15:30, negotiable).
